## Overview

IKOS-PIMS is a backend system built for **IKOS**, a German public transport operator, to manage passenger data across heterogeneous infrastructure environments.

The core design question this project answers: **can a high-performance C++ edge node and a JVM-based cloud node share a single source of truth without data corruption?**

The answer is yes — via **database-level pessimistic locking** on the shared PostgreSQL instance. Both services are operationally independent, speak the same REST contract, and target the same `pims_db` database. Neither service knows the other exists.

### What was built

- A **C++ backend** (Oatpp framework) — low-latency, memory-safe, built for resource-constrained edge hardware or on-board train servers
- A **Java backend** (Spring Boot 3.x) — JVM-based, ecosystem-rich, built for centralised cloud processing
- A **shared PostgreSQL 16** database instance — single source of truth with transactional integrity
- Full **Docker Compose** orchestration — one command brings up the entire system

---

## Architecture

### Dual-stack MVC

Both backends follow a standard **MVC / layered architecture**:

```
HTTP Request
     │
     ▼
┌─────────────┐
│  Controller │  ← handles HTTP, parses request, returns response
└──────┬──────┘
       │
       ▼
┌─────────────┐
│  Repository │  ← data access layer, talks directly to PostgreSQL
└──────┬──────┘
       │
       ▼
┌─────────────┐
│  PostgreSQL │  ← shared pims_db, pessimistic locking on writes
└─────────────┘
```

### System topology

```
                    ┌──────────────────────────┐
                    │     Client / Postman      │
                    └────┬─────────────────┬────┘
                         │                 │
              HTTP :8081  │                 │  HTTP :8082
                         │                 │
               ┌─────────▼──────┐  ┌───────▼──────────┐
               │  C++ Backend   │  │  Java Backend     │
               │  Oatpp         │  │  Spring Boot 3.x  │
               │  CMake + vcpkg │  │  Maven + JPA      │
               └─────────┬──────┘  └───────┬──────────┘
                         │                 │
                         └────────┬────────┘
                                  │
                         ┌────────▼────────┐
                         │   PostgreSQL 16  │
                         │   pims_db        │
                         │   port: 5432     │
                         └─────────────────┘
```

### Why two stacks?

| Concern | C++ (Oatpp) | Java (Spring Boot) |
|---|---|---|
| Target environment | Edge / on-board hardware | Cloud / centralised server |
| Memory model | RAII + smart pointers | JVM garbage collection |
| Concurrency | Async event loop | Managed thread pool |
| DB access | Native SQL via libpqxx | Spring Data JPA (Hibernate) |
| Build | CMake + vcpkg | Maven |
| Startup time | ~ms | ~seconds |
| Ecosystem | Lean, minimal deps | Rich, rapid development |

Both expose an **identical REST API contract** — a client can target either port interchangeably.

