## Getting Started

### Prerequisites

- Docker and Docker Compose
- Git

### One-command startup

```bash
git clone https://github.com/johdanike/ikos-pims.git
cd IKOS-PIMS
docker compose up --build -d
```

This single command will:
1. Pull PostgreSQL 16 and initialise `pims_db`
2. Compile the C++ binary inside Docker using native Ubuntu packages
3. Package and launch the Spring Boot JAR
4. Connect all three containers on a shared Docker network

### Verify services are running

```bash
# Check all containers are up
docker compose ps

# C++ edge node
curl http://localhost:8081/api/v1/passengers

# Java cloud node
curl http://localhost:8082/api/v1/passengers

# PostgreSQL direct access
docker exec -it <postgres-container> psql -U ikos_admin -d pims_db
```

---

## API Reference

Both backends honour the same REST contract. Target either port interchangeably.

### Register a passenger

```bash
# C++ edge node
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8081/api/v1/passengers \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"firstName": "Hananah", "lastName": "Musa"}'

# Java cloud node
curl -s -X POST http://localhost:8082/api/v1/passengers \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"firstName": "Herr", "lastName": "Emile"}'
```

**Response**
```json-java
{
  "id": "e4b3b2a1-1234-5678-9abc-def012345678",
  "firstName": "Hananah",
  "lastName": "Musa",
  "ticketStatus": "CONFIRMED"
}

json-c++
{
 "id": "e266337b-2526-9hsb-dfshjd6762728",
 "firstName": "Herr",
 "lastName": "Emile",
 "ticketStatus": "CONFIRMED"
}
```

### Get all passengers

```bash
curl -s http://localhost:8081/api/v1/passengers
curl -s http://localhost:8082/api/v1/passengers
```

### Get passenger by ID

```bash
curl -s http://localhost:8081/api/v1/passengers/<id>
curl -s http://localhost:8082/api/v1/passengers/<id>
```

